# tests/fixtures/ci.local.env — CI + local-test fixture.
#
# Drives `install.sh --build-only` in a temp dir for the install-render-stable
# gate. Must work for any operator's CI run — paths are placeholder strings,
# not real machine paths. CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR / CODEX_HOME are OVERRIDDEN at
# runtime by the test (via per-run env file) to a per-run mktemp dir, so the
# literals below are documentation of the contract; what matters in CI is that
# every substituted @@VAR@@ in active templates has a non-empty entry here.
#
# When you add a new @@VAR@@ to a template, you MUST add a matching entry
# here (and to templates/local.env.example, which advertises the contract to
# operators). The gate fails fast on missing vars via install.sh's existing
# empty-placeholder check.

# Per-harness build targets — overridden by the test at runtime, kept here
# so the file is self-documenting for operators reading it later.
CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=/tmp/que80-ci-claude-config
CODEX_HOME=/tmp/que80-ci-codex-home

# Path placeholders substituted into entrypoint templates by compile_entrypoint
# and into hook scripts by install_hook. install.sh scans each surface for
# @@[A-Z_]+@@ tokens and resolves them from the environment; an unset/empty
# var aborts the build via the empty-placeholder check. Adding a new template
# placeholder without an entry here is the bug class this gate catches at
# PR time (via the fixture-completeness assertion in
# tests/install-render-stable.test.sh, which reads this file directly so
# ambient CI env vars cannot mask a missing entry).
#
# AI_CONFIG_DIR is REQUIRED in the fixture even though install.sh defaults
# it from $repo_root (install.sh:76). The fixture-completeness assertion
# refuses to let the default mask a missing fixture entry — a future
# change to install.sh's default-resolution would otherwise silently leave
# a template surface relying on environment state CI may not provide.
AI_CONFIG_DIR=/tmp/que80-ci-agentic-os-template
OBSIDIAN_VAULT_PATH=/tmp/que80-ci-vault
